WEBVTT

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.490
Looks like preparation for a funeral is a lot of work...

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.630
...nii-sama.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:22.750
Onii-sama.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.500
Onii-sama!

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:26.860
Who is it?

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.060
Where are you?

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.570
Onii-sama, over here!

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.840
Who are you?

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:50.150
I'm... Onii-sama's little sister.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.110
Good morning, Onii-sama.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.090
What are you planning on doing so early in the morning?

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.030
What do you mean what?

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.510
Isn't it obvious I came to wake you up?

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.560
But why are you calling me "Onii-sama"?

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.270
Because we're siblings.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:50.820
That's true...

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.440
But saying it that way makes me remember that day.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.090
That day?

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.000
You know, the day of father's funeral service.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.950
Why did you feign innocence that day, Miyabi?

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.950
Feigning innocence...?

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:09.460
That's because my father said "Shougo-kun's father was the company president,

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:13.710
so if you don't mind your manners, he won't like you." So...

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:17.030
...that's why you said something so ill-suited.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.030
What do you mean, ill-suited?!

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:21.970
If I put my mind to it, I could become your subordinate!

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.100
Is something burning?

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:24.880
Ah!

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.100
Our breakfast!

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:38.280
It's breakfast... right?

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.820
Thanks for the food.

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:44.660
It was delicious.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:45.550
Huh?

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.310
Are you done already?

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:48.250
Yeah.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.040
Then, next is changing clothes, right?

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:50.790
Eh?

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.120
Wai- What are you...?

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.720
Hold still!

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.960
If you don't, I can't take your clothes off!

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.630
I don't need you to take them off!

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:00.870
No!

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.680
Are you planning on skipping school?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.200
Shougo-san, are you awake?

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.470
If you'd like, we could share some morning creampuff-

00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:09.080
Stop moving!

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.930
I told you not to take it off!

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.080
Ah!

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.440
W-What are you doing?!

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:21.440
Isn't it obvious?

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:23.750
Sibling skinship.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:24.450
Eh?

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:34.450
Hey, don't cling to me so much.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:35.710
What are you talking about?

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:37.330
That time...

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:39.850
Forgive you...?

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:41.380
We're siblings, aren't we?

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:47.680
That's right.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.520
We're siblings, right?

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:57.580
Miyabi, let's become even closer than lovers, as siblings.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.920
...it was you who said that, wasn't it, Shougo?

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:03.330
Well... it's true I said that, but...

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:04.190
Huh?

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.410
Ah!

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:17.600
Hey!

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.460
Cut it out!

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.300
I said cut it out!

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.050
Pia! Pia!

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:30.300
What are you doing so early in the morning?!

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.590
It's because we're siblings!

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.500
Mikadono, Kannagi.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.320
Why are your desks together?

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:52.120
I forgot to put my textbook into my bag.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.610
I see.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:54.830
Can't be helped, then.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:55.970
Yes!

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:57.960
It can't be helped.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:05.710
Here you go.

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:10.580
Today is your favourite, sweet omelettes and fried chicken.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:11.620
Oh!

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.040
It looks delicious!

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.600
Rather than that tiny one,

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:17.260
why don't you try this lunch that I put my best effort into?

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.640
Wait a second, Kunitachi-san.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.600
What do you mean by "that tiny one"?

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:24.860
There's no reason to ask, I meant exactly what you're thinking.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.360
Okay, stop.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:35.120
As Shougo's little sister, I'll decide which lunch is suitable for him.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.120
Okay, open up!

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.060
Delicious!

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:46.600
That suits my tastes.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:49.130
Next is Kunitachi-san's.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:51.510
Okay, open up!

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:53.350
Oh!

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:55.350
TL note: A type of chicken with expensive eggs.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:55.350
This is a silkie's egg!

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:58.090
This really brings out the flavour!

00:06:58.090 --> 00:07:00.650
Shougo, what do you want to eat next?

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:02.030
Let's see...

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:03.910
I think I'll have to go with the fried chicken.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:07.030
But that shrimp looks pretty tasty, too.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:08.330
Geez!

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.980
Then I guess I'll just have to feed you both!

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:12.770
Tsuruma-senpai.

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:16.380
There's something that I can't assent to.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:19.480
Kunitachi-san, I was thinking the same thing.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:24.790
Hold on a second, Kannagi-san.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:29.050
Why are you feeding him the lunches we made?!

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.800
Obviously it's because I'm Shougo's little sister.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:39.180
For your information, there's no way as his little sister I will allow someone I don't approve of to date Shougo.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.060
Wha-?!

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.230
Hey, Miyabi!

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.020
What are you talking about?

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.310
I see.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:49.440
So that means if Kannagi-san approves, you can date Shougo-kun?

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.320
Then, why don't we have a contest?

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:55.260
Sagara-senpai, what are you saying?

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:57.350
The candidates will go on dates with Mikadono,

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:01.080
and his little sister will watch and decide who is suitable for him.

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:03.840
It sounds like an interesting event, doesn't it?

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:08.350
Then we can have the candidates announce
their plans similar to a designing competition,

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:10.200
and evaluate them based on that.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:10.980
Oh!

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:12.590
That sounds really genuine!

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:15.180
Like I said before, what are you going on about?

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:15.930
Shougo-san?

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.220
W-What?

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.140
Is it true that if I get Kannagi-senpai to approve,

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:22.250
I'll be able to date you, Mikadono-senpai?

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:24.340
No, whether it's true and all of that...

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:25.330
It's true.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:25.770
Huh?

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:28.150
However.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:31.280
It won't be easy!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:37.700
Okay.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.110
First, we'll determine the order of the dates by drawing lots.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:44.790
Mana is first!

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:49.020
Why are you participating, President Tendou?

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:51.420
Well, because it sounds fun!

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:55.290
Besides, Shougo-kun's company is big, right?

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:59.930
If we get married, I'll be able to buy lots of sweets!

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:01.580
President Tendou.

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:04.860
If you would please announce your date plans.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.940
Mana's date will be...

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:11.220
Winning over his heart in the candy land!

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:17.180
Everything's cheap, it's all cheap!

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:20.440
Please take a look at anything you'd like.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.450
This is the candy land?

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:24.150
Look, look!

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:26.290
There's lots of candy!

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:29.900
Look, look!

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:32.460
If you see anything you like, put it into the basket!

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:34.020
Yeah...

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:41.470
This is the next place?

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.770
Yep.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:45.620
Geez...

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:48.380
She's only going to places related to sweets.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:50.980
Well, that's just like her.

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:54.740
Places like this are unexpectedly good for-

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:56.740
T-These are...

00:09:57.190 --> 00:10:02.210
The potato chips that went on sale 15 years ago and sold out instantly!

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:04.240
The legendary salmiakki flavour!

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:06.580
Granny, I'd like to buy these!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:07.330
Wait a second!

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:11.410
If they were from 15 years ago, they're way past their expiration date!

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:20.400
How are you supposed to eat this suspicious-looking thing?

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.590
"Suspicious"?

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:23.680
Good grief.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:24.260
Huh?

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:28.130
Kids these days don't even know how to eat a monja?

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.670
Kotori-sensei.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:32.120
Why are you here?

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:33.580
Why indeed?

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:36.540
Because this is my favourite place.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:39.530
I come here because they put it on my tab.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:46.670
Pres?

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:47.590
What's that?

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:51.240
This is a special menu for regulars only.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:10:59.970
Could it be, is that...?

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:01.220
That's right!

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.970
It's a hotcake!

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.480
Here.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:22.680
How is it?

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:23.760
Is it good?

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:24.530
Yes.

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:26.370
It's a very nostalgic flavour.

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:27.770
I see.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:29.120
Glad to hear that.

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:42.180
If I got married to President Tendou,

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:45.440
I wonder if every day would have this peaceful feeling?

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:48.730
Darling!

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:50.770
Dinner is ready!

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:55.480
Hotcakes again today?

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.980
They're delicious, but if you eat them every day...

00:11:57.980 --> 00:11:59.140
Eh?

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:02.750
Then... How about this for today?

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:16.780
Yes... Just like that.

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:21.920
They bruise easily, so do it gently, okay?

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.300
Like that.

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:37.770
...Or something like that.

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.940
Okay, that's enough!

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:43.670
Hey!

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:03.420
Next is my turn.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:08.430
My date concept is plans for the future.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:16.280
Why are you participating, Sagara-senpai?

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:17.440
Isn't it obvious?

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:23.440
Getting married to you is the quickest
way to watch over Miyabi from nearby.

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:25.700
"The quickest way"...?

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:30.010
"Café Demon Eyes"...?

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:35.210
Um... This kind of has an unpleasant feel to it...

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:46.720
Huh?

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:50.310
So, thou hast finally come.

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:53.720
We who art the kin of darkness, deeper thanst jet black midnight.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:55.190
Club President Araya!

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:55.980
What are you doing here?

00:13:55.980 --> 00:14:00.070
Ah... The newspaper club's funds were running low,

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:01.730
so we're working here part-time.

00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:03.530
Even Yuu-san is here...

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:06.790
Now, ye summoned kin,

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:10.910
make thine choice of smoking or non-smoking sections.

00:14:15.030 --> 00:14:17.790
Let's do it, Ganizeus!

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:21.280
Restructuring Warrior, Gran Belion!

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:26.320
"Café Special Effects"...?

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:35.610
Onii-sama, thanks for your hard work on making your appearance at this shop.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:43.520
What is it, Mikadono?

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.800
According to my research, you should like this.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:47.610
Eh?

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:50.110
Well... yeah.

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:56.580
"Café Married Life"...?

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:04.870
Welcome home, darling.

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:07.260
Would you like to have dinner?

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:08.340
Or a bath?

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.360
Or perhaps...

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:13.240
Oh...

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:20.350
Welcome home, Onii-chan!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:25.360
So, why are we ending the date at your shop?

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:31.110
Because if you marry me, you'll become the co-owner of this shop.

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:35.120
So for the last destination of our date, there's no place more suitable.

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:38.140
So this is what you meant by "plans for the future".

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:46.880
But... if I married Sagara-senpai, it could be like that Married Life Café.

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:53.050
I'm home.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:00.890
Welcome home, darling.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.530
Would you like to have dinner?

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:04.270
Or a bath?

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:08.570
Or perhaps... a scouring pad?

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:13.580
Senpai, why is it a scouring pad?!

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:15.130
What are you talking about?

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:16.560
I don't understand what you mean.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:17.950
Okay, that's enough!

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:22.710
Shougo, you were thinking something dirty, weren't you?

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:26.710
Hey, wait!

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:29.920
Next is my turn.

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:35.680
My date concept is... a memorable date.

00:16:57.280 --> 00:17:03.050
W-Well, this certainly is a memorable date for a high school student.

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:05.760
Yeah, there's no mistaking that.

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:10.070
But I have a feeling there's something really wrong with this.

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:15.180
I don't really get it, but the mood is too good, so I can't allow it!

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:28.040
Next is my turn, right?

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:29.400
The concept is...

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:36.830
Good grief, Father.

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:38.970
Only talking about old times...

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:40.290
Don't say it like that.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:44.160
Any father would be surprised if you
suddenly say you're bringing your lover over.

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:47.950
Darling, isn't it about time?

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:49.420
Oh, I guess so.

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:54.380
Well then, we'll leave you two young ones alone.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:18:00.680
Kunitachi-san said the concept of the date was "Japanese style", but...

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:03.060
But however you look at it...

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:08.440
This is a marriage interview, isn't it?!

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:12.470
Come on Shougo, we're going!

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:13.260
Wait!

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:15.490
My date is not over yet!

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.420
You're withdrawn!

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:20.740
If we just go along with this, we already know what will happen.

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:23.460
H-Hey, Miyabi...

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:33.120
I'm the last one, right?

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:38.630
My date concept... is this!

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:39.880
Huh?

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:42.390
Come on, let's go together.

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:43.020
Huh?

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:45.140
Eh? Wait a sec...

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:26.930
Hey!

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:52.210
This is...

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:53.250
Yes.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:54.580
It's a pretend wedding ceremony.

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:59.010
They're doing a bridal experience fare here,

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:01.890
and you can try on a wedding dress.

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:10.700
Kannagi-san, we've decided the order to try on dresses.

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:12.100
Let's go to the dressing room.

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:18.350
There are more designs for wedding dresses than you would think, aren't there?

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:21.210
So many I can't decide which I want to try on!

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:23.820
What kind do you want to try, Kannagi-san?

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:26.750
The one from just before was pretty cute, wasn't it?

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:32.390
I wonder if I should just go with the classic type?

00:20:32.390 --> 00:20:33.250
Huh?

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:37.680
Kannagi-san?

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:42.880
Sorry for the wait!

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:46.510
I brought your bride for you, Onii-sama.

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:05.590
Next couple, go ahead.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:35.690
All right, I'm ready.

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:46.450
Say cheese!

00:21:52.530 --> 00:21:55.080
Now it's our turn!

00:21:58.800 --> 00:21:59.830
Eh?

